---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/evohq.css';

export const prerender = true;
---

<BaseLayout title="LLM work and research" description="Open LLM-related work, selected merged patches, projects, and research writing by Atharva Kanherkar." canonical="https://www.atharvakanherkar.com/evohq">
  <article class="evohq">
    <header class="evohq__hero">
      <p class="evohq__eyebrow">Atharva Kanherkar</p>
      <h1>LLM work and research</h1>
      <p>A small public index of things I am working on, things I have merged, and writing around model gateways, agents, and evaluation.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="evohq__section" aria-labelledby="open-work">
      <p class="evohq__label">Open work</p>
      <h2 id="open-work">Open pull requests</h2>
      <div class="evohq__list">
        <a href="https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Gym/pull/2437"><span>NVIDIA NeMo Gym</span><strong>Aggregate metrics helper for agents</strong><small>Open PR</small></a>
        <a href="https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/labs-OO-Agents/pull/115"><span>NVIDIA NeMo OO Agents</span><strong>Make sync agent methods respect middleware</strong><small>Open PR</small></a>
      </div>

      <h2 class="evohq__subhead">Open issues</h2>
      <div class="evohq__list evohq__list--issues">
        <a href="https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Switchyard/issues/423"><span>Switchyard</span><strong>Do not echo a base URL containing a key in a 502</strong><small>Open issue</small></a>
        <a href="https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Switchyard/issues/410"><span>Switchyard</span><strong>Do not pass client <code>x-*</code> headers upstream</strong><small>Open issue</small></a>
        <a href="https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/labs-OO-Agents/issues/114"><span>NVIDIA NeMo OO Agents</span><strong>Sync agent methods skip <code>agent_call</code> middleware</strong><small>Open issue</small></a>
        <a href="https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm/issues/37118"><span>LiteLLM</span><strong>Messages endpoint drops stop sequences</strong><small>Open issue</small></a>
        <a href="https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm/issues/36794"><span>LiteLLM</span><strong>Proxy accepts a request-body API key when it should not</strong><small>Open issue</small></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="evohq__section" aria-labelledby="merged-work">
      <p class="evohq__label">Recently merged</p>
      <h2 id="merged-work">A few upstream fixes</h2>
      <div class="evohq__merged">
        <article><span>NVIDIA NeMo / Switchyard</span><h3>Kept system and developer messages as instructions when routing Responses API calls.</h3><a href="https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Switchyard/pull/523">View PR ↗</a></article>
        <article><span>NVIDIA NeMo / Switchyard</span><h3>Stopped clients from forwarding API keys and OpenAI tenant headers through the proxy.</h3><a href="https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Switchyard/pull/420">View PR ↗</a></article>
        <article><span>NVIDIA NeMo / Switchyard</span><h3>Made content-filtered replies show up correctly for Anthropic clients.</h3><a href="https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Switchyard/pull/370">View PR ↗</a></article>
        <article><span>Mozilla AI / AnyLLM</span><h3>Fixed a Messages bridge that could leave out thinking, tool, attachments, and schema details.</h3><a href="https://github.com/mozilla-ai/any-llm/pull/1312">View PR ↗</a></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="evohq__section" aria-labelledby="projects">
      <p class="evohq__label">Projects</p>
      <h2 id="projects">Things I have built around this work</h2>
      <div class="evohq__projects">
        <a href="https://github.com/Atharva-Kanherkar/kairo"><b>Kairo</b><span>A research dataset and test harness for LLM gateway translation. It collects real breakages and makes them easier to replay across gateways.</span></a>
        <a href="https://github.com/agentclash/agentclash"><b>AgentClash</b><span>Agent evaluation for real tasks, comparisons, and regressions.</span></a>
        <a href="https://github.com/agentclash/agentic-memory"><b>agentic-memory</b><span>Separate semantic, episodic, and procedural memory for agents.</span></a>
        <a href="https://github.com/Atharva-Kanherkar/datasmith"><b>datasmith</b><span>Tools for building synthetic data and evaluation datasets.</span></a>
        <a href="https://github.com/Atharva-Kanherkar/proofswe"><b>ProofSWE</b><span>A way to capture and score coding-agent sessions.</span></a>
        <a href="https://github.com/Atharva-Kanherkar/chalkboard"><b>chalkboard</b><span>A prompt-to-explainer-video tool that can run with local models.</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="evohq__section" aria-labelledby="rimo-work">
      <p class="evohq__label">Work</p>
      <h2 id="rimo-work">The last six months at Rimo</h2>
      <p class="evohq__copy">I have worked on model-connected product features, agent tools, OAuth and connector flows, and the background jobs and privacy checks around knowledge extraction. I have also worked on evaluation and model-selection work. This section stays high level because the underlying work is private.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="evohq__section" aria-labelledby="writing">
      <p class="evohq__label">Writing</p>
      <h2 id="writing">Research notes on X</h2>
      <p class="evohq__copy">I write longer notes on <a href="https://x.com/attharrva15/articles">X Articles</a>. A few recent ones:</p>
      <div class="evohq__writing">
        <a href="https://x.com/attharrva15/status/2095194553397739728"><span>LLM routers and related research</span><strong>A look at gateway translation problems, with Kairo as a way to collect and replay the failures.</strong></a>
        <a href="https://x.com/attharrva15/status/2088234380724690972"><span>Your LLM proxy’s health check is handing out your API keys</span><strong>Two reproducible credential problems in LiteLLM and Switchyard, explained with the requests that made them visible.</strong></a>
        <a href="https://x.com/attharrva15/status/2087817964783649154"><span>You are probably wrong about open intelligence</span><strong>Notes from trying lower-cost models in agent work, and why open data and useful evaluation matter as much as open weights.</strong></a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
